# {{name}} MCP server

MCP tools for **{{title}}** ({{api_version}}), generated from an OpenAPI document by
openapi-to-mcp {{generator_version}} (crew-chief-middleware).

- Base URL: `{{base_url}}`
- Authentication: `{{auth_kind}}` (credentials from environment variables only)
- Tools: {{tool_count}}

## Run it

```bash
python -m venv .venv && . .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
cp .env.example .env      # fill in credentials, keep it out of git
set -a && . ./.env && set +a
python server.py          # speaks MCP over stdio
```

The process reads MCP JSON-RPC on stdin and writes it on stdout, so it looks idle
when you start it by hand. Logs go to stderr.

## Connect an MCP client

Copy `mcp.example.json` into your client config (Cursor: `~/.cursor/mcp.json`, or
`.cursor/mcp.json` in a project), replace the placeholder path with the absolute
path to `server.py`, and provide credentials the way your client supports —
inherited environment, its `env` block, or a secret manager. Do not commit a
config file containing real credentials; `mcp.json` is git-ignored here.

## Configuration

| Environment variable | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
{{credential_env_docs}}
| `{{env_prefix}}_BASE_URL` | override the API base URL |
| `{{env_prefix}}_READ_ONLY` | expose only non-mutating tools |
| `{{env_prefix}}_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | per-request timeout (default 30) |
| `{{env_prefix}}_MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES` | response cap before truncation (default 100000) |
| `{{env_prefix}}_MAX_RETRIES` | retries for idempotent requests on 429/502/503/504 (default 2) |
| `{{env_prefix}}_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP` | allow plaintext http to a non-loopback host |
| `{{env_prefix}}_LOG_LEVEL` | stderr log level (default WARNING) |

